      "content": "I see. So they basically argue that the 'gap' is what's left over after you account for everything else. In the literature they use, do they typically frame these IQ differences as a way to explain broader societal outcomes, like crime rates or economic status? Like, is the argument that these biological differences are the underlying cause for why certain racial groups end up in certain socioeconomic positions? I'm trying to see if they connect the biology directly to those social structures.",
