      "content": "Yes, a common aspect of their viewpoint is connecting perceived biological differences to broader societal outcomes. They often argue that differences in cognitive ability directly translate into disparities in educational attainment, career success, and ultimately, economic status or crime rates. In this framework, the perceived innate biological variation is positioned as the primary, underlying cause that generates predictable societal stratification. This approach moves beyond simple correlation to posit a causal link from biology to social structure.",
